      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture of the test. The main understandability issues are:\n1. Many unused imports and class-level fields/methods that are irrelevant to `testSerialization`\n2. Unclear variable names (`shortRec`, `rec`, `object`)\n3. Inline comments explain what, not why\n\nI'll write an improved version now.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports, fields, and setup infrastructure, renames `shortRec`/`rec` to `original`/`deserialized` for clarity, and replaces terse inline comments with explanations of *why* each assertion group matters."
